From 353d3054a556f94b6b45be7802b9965084629b4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:15:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add PowerPC thread state support to the XNU debugger

* Read and write GPRs via `PPC_THREAD_STATE` or `PPC_THREAD_STATE64` by debuggee cpu type
* Single-step via MSR[SE] in srr1, ppc has no debug state flavor
* Enable the Mach exception port path on ppc
* Decode exception codes in native byte order, they were read as little endian
* Fix ppc register aliases and add a ppc64 register profile

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by agent: Claude Code/Claude Opus 5.5
